 cmd/curator	TestEnvStatusReportsLockedRequire	linux,darwin,windows	-	-	env status reports the locked require_current_profile in JSON and text
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# Real-pnpm integration -- Windows store-registry gap (BUG-260916-2f3xbf)
+#
+# The pnpm pin (TASK-260916-5aqozl) installs pnpm 10.33.0 in every suite lane
+# so the three TestRealPinnedPNPM* cases execute instead of skipping. On
+# windows-latest two of them fail with `closure_input_undeclared: pnpm
+# writable store registry contains an undeclared member` (gate run 35098955988):
+# pnpm writes a store member on Windows that the closure registry does not
+# declare. That is a product gap, not a CI gap, filed as BUG-260916-2f3xbf.
+#
+# Until the bug lands, exactly these two cases are Windows-deferred: required
+# on linux,darwin, where they pass against the pinned pnpm, and tolerating the
+# bug-naming stage-deferred skip on windows only. A skip of either case on a
+# unix runner, or for any other reason on Windows, is fatal. The third case
+# (TestRealPinnedPNPMTargetPrunedUnreachableRejectsBeforeInstall) passes on all
+# three runners and carries no row. Removal: BUG-260916-2f3xbf's AC is green on
+# windows-latest with no ledger deferral -- widen must_run_on to windows and
+# delete the Go skip with it.
+# ===========================================================================
+internal/pnpmsource	TestRealPinnedPNPMLockSupersetSnapshotDependencies	linux,darwin	windows	stage-deferred	pinned-pnpm lock-superset case executes on unix; deferred on windows pending BUG-260916-2f3xbf (undeclared writable-store member), asserted there once the bug lands
+internal/pnpmsource	TestRealPinnedPNPMPrivateStoreAndOfflineMaterialization	linux,darwin	windows	stage-deferred	pinned-pnpm private-store and offline-materialization case executes on unix; deferred on windows pending BUG-260916-2f3xbf (undeclared writable-store member), asserted there once the bug lands
diff --git a/.github/ci/pnpm-pin-guard.sh b/.github/ci/pnpm-pin-guard.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..014de0e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.github/ci/pnpm-pin-guard.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# pnpm pin guard: the workflow's PNPM_PIN must name exactly the release
+# internal/pnpmsource admits, or the lane stops before installing anything.
+#
+# The Go constant internal/pnpmsource.SupportedPNPMVersion is the single
+# source of truth; the workflow-level `env: PNPM_PIN` is a copy of it, kept
+# as a copy (rather than extracted at install time) so the installed release
+# is visible in the workflow and in every job log. This script is what keeps
+# the copy honest: a Go-side bump that forgets the workflow fails the lane
+# here, instead of installing the old pnpm and skipping (or failing) the
+# real-pnpm integration tests downstream.
+#
+# A read failure is never a match: an unset pin, an unreadable source file,
+# or a source file with no declaration all fail closed.
+#
+# Usage:
+#   PNPM_PIN=10.33.0 bash .github/ci/pnpm-pin-guard.sh
+#
+# Self-test override:
+#   CI_PNPM_GO_SOURCE  Go source to read the constant from
+#                      (default: internal/pnpmsource/errors.go)
+
+set -u
+
+fail() { echo "pnpm-pin: $*" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+[ -n "${PNPM_PIN:-}" ] || fail 'PNPM_PIN is not set; the workflow must export the pinned pnpm release'
+
+src="${CI_PNPM_GO_SOURCE:-internal/pnpmsource/errors.go}"
+[ -r "$src" ] || fail "cannot read $src"
+
+line="$(grep -E 'SupportedPNPMVersion[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*"' "$src" | head -n 1)"
+[ -n "$line" ] || fail "no SupportedPNPMVersion declaration in $src"
+go_pin="$(printf '%s' "$line" | sed -n 's/.*SupportedPNPMVersion[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p')"
+[ -n "$go_pin" ] || fail "cannot parse SupportedPNPMVersion from $src"
+
+[ "$PNPM_PIN" = "$go_pin" ] || fail "workflow PNPM_PIN=$PNPM_PIN disagrees with internal/pnpmsource SupportedPNPMVersion=$go_pin"
+
+printf 'pnpm-pin: workflow and Go agree on pnpm %s\n' "$PNPM_PIN"
